      "data": {
        "value": "<p>Clinical history &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;K/C/O Multiple myeloma<br>Specimen &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Bone marrow<br>Instrument software&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; BD FACS LYRIC/BD FACS SUITE<br>Gating strategy &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;10 colour FCM using FSC vs.CD45&amp;CD38-CD138 gating<br>Cell preparation method&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Stain - Lyse - Wash<br>Number of Events Acquired&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 440731<br>FSC SSC Viable events&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; 334766</p>\n<p><br>Descriptive Summary:- The flow cytometry examination of bone marrow was done. A total of 4.4 lac events were acquired.</p>\n<p>The analysis shows a cluster of normal polyclonal plasma cells &nbsp;2.98% of all viable gated cells.</p>\n<p><br>These normal plasma cells show normal expression of CD38, CD138, CD27, CD81 and polyclonal light chain expression and are negative for CD117 and CD56.</p>\n<table class=\"Table cke_show_border\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99%; border-spacing: 0px;\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" data-cke-table-faked-selection-table=\"\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><strong>Minimal Residual disease not detected.</strong><br><br><br><strong>Total plasma cells,% of viable cells</strong></td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><br><br><br>2.98</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><br><br><br>%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><strong>NPC,% of viable cells</strong><br>(Normal plasma cells)</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\">2.98</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\">%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\"><strong>APC,% of viable cells</strong><br>(Abnormal plasma cells)</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\">0.0000</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\">%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><strong>IMPRESSION: Flow cytometry analysis does not show evidence of minimal residual disease</strong><br><br></p>\n<table class=\"Table cke_show_border\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99%; border-spacing: 0px;\" border=\"1\" cellspacing=\"0\" data-cke-table-faked-selection-table=\"\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\">Limit Of Detection (LOD)</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\">0.0060</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\">%</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\">Limit Of Quantification (LOQ)</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\">0.0149</td>\n<td class=\"cke_table-faked-selection\" style=\"padding: 1px;\">%</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><br><strong>Note: </strong>In the above MRD assay for calculation of limit of detection (LOD) a threshold of 20 events is used and for calculation of limit of quantification (LOQ) a threshold of 50 events is used.<br>MRD results are to be correlated with the clinical details, diagnostic immunophenotype and cytogenetic profile of the patient. MRD can be used as an independent prognostic factor for the patient, however its role for therapeutic decisions is to be based on the treatment protocol being used for the patient.</p>",
